                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                  %mo :
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi c
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_{c,c'} : F(c \otimes c') \to F(c) \otimes F(c')
          %p
            which must satisfy a certain
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence+law"} coherence law
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            An oplax monoidal functor sends
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonoids"} comonoids
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to comonoids in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoids"} monoids
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to monoids in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "." do
              %strong lax comonoidal functor
            %strong colax monoidal
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %strong lax opmonoidal
          %p
            Note that a
            %em strong
            opmonoidal functor –in which the morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            are required to be
            = succeed "\u2014" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
          #OplaxAdjointToLax.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A functor with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              is oplax monoidal if and only if that right adjoint is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              This is a special case of the statement of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/doctrinal+adjunction"} doctrinal adjunction
              for the case of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monad"} 2-monad
              whose algebras are monoidal categories,
          %p Here is the explicit construction of the oplax monoidal structure from a lax monoidal structure on a right adjoint:
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi L
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L \dashv R) : C \stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{R}{\to}} D
            be a pair of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\otimes)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (D,\otimes)
            be structures of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
          %p
            Then if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            becomes an oplax monoidal functor with oplax unit
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi I
                    %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi I
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  L(I_D) \to I_C
          %p
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
            of the lax unit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi I
                    %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi I
                    %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_D \to R(I_D)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            and with oplax monoidal transformation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (L (x \otimes y) \stackrel{\Delta_{x,y}}{\to} L(x) \otimes L(y))
          %p
            given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
            of
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi y
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi x
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi y
                  %mi R
                  %mi L
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi R
                  %mi L
                  %mi y
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∇
                        %mrow
                          %mi L
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi L
                          %mi y
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi L
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  x \otimes y \stackrel{\eta_x \otimes \eta_y}{\to}
                  R L x \otimes R L y
                  \\stackrel{\nabla_{L x, L y}}{\to}
                  R(L x \otimes L y)
                  \\,.
          %p
            By the formula for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjuncts"} adjuncts
            in terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+counit"} adjunction counit
            (
            %a{:href => "adjunct#AdjunctionCoUnitGiveesAllAdjuncts"}> this prop.
            ) this adjunct is the composite
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi x
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mi L
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi R
                  %mi L
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mo ∇
                        %mrow
                          %mi L
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi L
                          %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi L
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi L
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mrow
                          %mi L
                          %mi x
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi L
                          %mi y
                  %mi L
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi L
                  %mi y
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  L(x \otimes y)
                  \\stackrel{L(\eta_x \otimes \eta_y)}{\longrightarrow}
                  L(R L x \otimes R L y)
                  \\stackrel{L(\nabla_{L x, L y})}{\longrightarrow}
                  L R(L x \otimes L y)
                  \\stackrel{\epsilon_{L x \otimes L y}}{\longrightarrow}
                  L x \otimes L y
                  \\,.
          %p
            This appears for instance on
            %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0209/0209342v2.pdf#page=17"} p. 17
            of (
            %a{:href => "#SchwedeShipley"}> SchwedeShipley
            ).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+functor"} monoidal functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
            %li
              %p
                %strong oplax monoidal functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilax+monoidal+functor"} bilax monoidal functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+monoidal+functor"} Frobenius monoidal functor
          %h2#references References
          %p The construction of oplax monoidal functors from right adjoint lax monoidal functors is considered for instance around page 17 of
          %ul#SchwedeShipley
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
              %em Equivalences of monoidal model categories
              , Algebr. Geom. Topol. 3 (2003), 287–334 (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0209342"}> arXiv
              )
